  "generated_text": "To determine Melanie's average speed for her entire run, we need to calculate the total distance she ran and the total time she took to run that distance. The average speed is then the total distance divided by the total time.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the time taken for each segment of the run:\n\n1. **First segment:**\n   - Distance: \\(400\\) meters\n   - Speed: \\(5\\) m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{400 \\text{ meters}}{5 \\text{ m/s}} = 80 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\n2. **Second segment:**\n   - Distance: \\(800\\) meters\n   - Speed: \\(4\\) m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{800 \\text{ meters}}{4 \\text{ m/s}} = 200 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\n3. **Third segment:**\n   - Distance: \\(400\\) meters\n   - Speed: \\(8\\) m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{400 \\text{ meters}}{8 \\text{ m/s}} = 50 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\nNext, we sum the times for all three segments to get the total time:\n\\[\n80 \\text{ seconds} + 200 \\text{ seconds} + 50 \\text{ seconds} = 330 \\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the total distance:\n\\[\n400 \\text{ meters} + 800 \\text{ meters} + 400 \\text{ meters} = 1600 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find the average speed by dividing the total distance by the total time:\n\\[\n\\text{Average speed} = \\frac{1600 \\text{ meters}}{330 \\text{ seconds}}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1600 and 330. Using the Euclidean algorithm:\n\n\\[\n1600 \\div 330 \\approx 4.8485 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 4)}\n\\]\n\\[\n1600 - 4 \\times 330 = 1600 - 1320 = 280\n\\]\n\\[\n330 \\div 280 \\approx 1.1786 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n330 - 1 \\times 280 = 330 - 280 = 50\n\\]\n\\[\n280 \\div 50 = 5.6 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 5)}\n\\]\n\\[\n280 - 5 \\times 50 = 280 - 250 = 30\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\div 30 = 1.6667 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n50 - 1 \\times 30 = 50 - 30 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n30 \\div 20 = 1.5 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n30 - 1 \\times 20 = 30 - 20 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n20 \\div 10 = 2 \\quad \\text{(integer part is 2)}\n\\]\n\\[\n20 - 2 \\times 10 = 20 - 20 = 0\n\\]\n\nThe GCD is 10. We divide both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction \\(\\frac{1600}{330}\\) by 10:\n\\[\n\\frac{1600 \\div 10}{330 \\div 10} = \\frac{160}{33}\n\\]\n\nThus, Melanie's average speed is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{160}{33}}\n\\]",
